cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Trustabl in your work, please cite it as below."
title: Trustabl
abstract: >-
  Trustabl finds and fixes reliability, safety, and security defects in AI-agent
  codebases. It discovers a repository's agent and tool inventory with
  tree-sitter, runs YAML-defined detection rules against it, reports weaknesses
  as a human summary, JSON, or SARIF 2.1.0, and can apply the fixes to source.
  Scanning is fully local and deterministic - no LLM, no network, no code upload.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Trustabl
    website: "https://trustabl.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/trustabl/trustabl"
url: "https://trustabl.ai"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.7
date-released: "2026-08-14"
keywords:
  - agent-reliability
  - ai-agents
  - static-analysis
  - sarif
  - mcp
